Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on **Calls** here and on the Fleet home page.

## Interview call reminders (release 41)

For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day''s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or **Call** for a phone call). **Today** shows **Interviews today**: each call''s time, candidate, role and its **Join** or **Call** button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.

## The Sales funnel (release 48)

The Pipeline tab opens with **Sales funnel**.

1. **Sales staff in the academy**: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows "Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago". A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.
2. **The re-send**: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as **Yes, put me in Sales**, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.
3. **The bar for Sales**: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI''s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.
4. A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in **Settings** > **Program**.

## Interview calls in the site (release 50)

A video interview is now a private call inside the site, one room per slot, in place of the Jitsi link. The candidate''s booking email (with a calendar invite) has their own link: it opens the call in their browser with no account, and works in one browser only (another browser is refused; a moved or cancelled call''s link stops working). Opening the candidate yourself never uses their link: on the candidate''s page press **Join the interview call**. Their details, answers, the role''s questions and the rubric are beside the video, with **No show** and **Not hired**; Hire and the decision email stay on the candidate''s page.

The weekly townhall is a call in the site too (Townhall, **Join the call**): you present, your slide is everyone''s, and People shows who is in the call, who left and who has not joined. Attendance is recorded by itself. If the media server is down, **Switch to the outside link** on the Townhall page sends everyone to the link in Program settings until you switch back.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role&#39;s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.</p><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-open-a-role-and-send-the-apply-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Open a role and send the apply link</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the role</b> to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); <b class="gd-ui">Close the role</b> takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role&#39;s questions, about five minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pass mark and pay</b> changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-what-happens-to-each-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens to each application</h2><p class="gd-p">The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).</li><li>Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so. The email&#39;s button is <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>: one press makes their Sales application from the one they sent (no new form) and sends the AI interview link at once.</li><li>Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.</li><li>A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.</li><li>Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-review-the-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review the applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Applications.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite anyway</b> sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview days</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Interview days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. A short form opens: the <b class="gd-ui">Role</b> (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the <b class="gd-ui">Start date</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, filled in with the role&#39;s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm: hire and start onboarding</b>. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do&#39;s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email (release 44: no start date in it; training and claiming shifts only, then a hello in the team chat and the member tag &quot;Name - Position&quot; in each WhatsApp group, also a first-day To do); their call slot and AI interview link close.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire&#39;s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line and the answer&#39;s score out of 10. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The interview decides by itself (release 41, on by default again since release 44): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b> on any candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b> holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and <b class="gd-ui">Decide by hand</b> if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-redo-the-ai-interview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Redo the AI interview</h2><p class="gd-p">If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant&#39;s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Redo the AI interview</b>, then confirm.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Their staff access ends if they were already hired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The application goes back to <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b> and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-in-person-needs-the-toronto-area-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list and the candidate page show <b class="gd-ui">Lives in</b>, flag <b class="gd-ui">Location mismatch</b> when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer <b class="gd-ui">Move to Remote Sales</b> to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-dates-before-the-townhall-release-35-widened-in-re" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> here and on the Fleet home page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-call-reminders-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview call reminders (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day&#39;s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> for a phone call). <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Interviews today</b>: each call&#39;s time, candidate, role and its <b class="gd-ui">Join</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-the-sales-funnel-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Sales funnel (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Pipeline tab opens with <b class="gd-ui">Sales funnel</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sales staff in the academy</b>: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows &quot;Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago&quot;. A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The re-send</b>: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The bar for Sales</b>: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI&#39;s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-calls-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview calls in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">A video interview is now a private call inside the site, one room per slot, in place of the Jitsi link. The candidate&#39;s booking email (with a calendar invite) has their own link: it opens the call in their browser with no account, and works in one browser only (another browser is refused; a moved or cancelled call&#39;s link stops working). Opening the candidate yourself never uses their link: on the candidate&#39;s page press <b class="gd-ui">Join the interview call</b>. Their details, answers, the role&#39;s questions and the rubric are beside the video, with <b class="gd-ui">No show</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b>; Hire and the decision email stay on the candidate&#39;s page.</p><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a call in the site too (Townhall, <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b>): you present, your slide is everyone&#39;s, and People shows who is in the call, who left and who has not joined. Attendance is recorded by itself. If the media server is down, <b class="gd-ui">Switch to the outside link</b> on the Townhall page sends everyone to the link in Program settings until you switch back.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'your-workday', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.

## The menu

Every office role has the same short menu: **To do** (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one **More** for the rest of your work, **Bookings** (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and **Me** (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: **Send an offer** and **New quote** on Requests, **Add a rental** on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters'' phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.

A **More** page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.

| Function | Your links, then More |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur |
| Sales | Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur |
| Fleet | Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button) |
| Finance | Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills |

## To do

Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.

1. The top shows your function, today''s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.
2. **Next up** is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or **Take it** to make it yours.
3. Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.
4. Customer service and Sales: **Waiting for a reply** lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today''s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.
5. **Every open task**: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.
6. Press **Take it** to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. **Sheet** opens the step-by-step procedure.
7. Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day''s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.
8. On a computer, press **/** to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 48.6 20.2, 2 31.9 52.1, 3 41.7 72.3")

## Work a task

Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.

| Button | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Open the working screen** | Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about. |
| **Done** | You finished it. It leaves the queue. |
| **Waiting** | You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours. |
| **Escalate** | It needs an Admin. Add why. |
| **Hand over** | Give it to someone else on the team. |
| **Add a note** | Leave a note for whoever looks next. |

> Tip: Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.

## Today

1. Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.
2. Press a booking number to open it. **To do** takes you back to your tasks.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 700; address: carmacars.ca/va/today; pins: 1 22.9 24.6")

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. The queue shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Several functions? Switch with Working as

If you cover more than one function, **Working as** above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.

## Your scorecard

1. Open **Me** (the **Scorecard** tab).
2. By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.
4. The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 360; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 1 4.2 39.7, 2 62.5 58.3")

## Clock in and out

Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press **Clock in** on your home page when you start and **Clock out** when you stop. **My hours** shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.

## Breaks and activity (release 35)

Take breaks when you need them: there is no fixed length. Press **Start break** next to the clock (a reason is optional) and **End break** when you are back. The timer shows how long the break has run; after 30 minutes you get a reminder and the Admins see it. Clocking out ends a break. Your breaks are on **My hours**; only an Admin can change one, with the reason.

While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks **Still there?**: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the **Call** button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first (sign it on Welcome or Documents to sign), then the academy, then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show your WhatsApp groups (Sales: CARMA Closers and the CarmaCars Team; everyone else the Team group). Next to each link is your member tag, written for you as "Name - Position" (for example "Darren - Sales"), with **Copy member tag** and the steps: open the group, tap its name, tap your own name (or Edit member tag), paste and save. Join each group and set the tag, then press **I joined** and tick **I set my member tag**: I joined does not go through without it.

Passed the Sales part of the academy while Sales is not your main role? Your home page shows the Sales group (CARMA Closers) too: join it and set your tag the same way.

No progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.

## The weekly townhall

**Me** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call''s deck, the next call time and its link. **Add to my calendar** adds the call every week.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)

**KPIs by week** sits on **My scorecard**: your role''s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.

## Your schedule, hours and pay

**Hours** > **Schedule** shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.

| Role | Schedule |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | 6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off |
| Finance | Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work |
| Fleet | 6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off |

1. Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.
2. You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under **Hours** > **My hours**, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.
3. Finance prepares the payroll under **Hours** > **Payroll**: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then **Send for approval**. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.

## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.

## Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)

- Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval.
- Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.
- Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.
- Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.', 'Your workday', 'The menu, To do, task actions, Today, switching functions and your scorecard.',
