## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.

## Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)

- Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval.
- Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.
- Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.
- Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.

## The townhall call in the site (release 50)

The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press **Join the call** on **Townhall** or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then **Join the call** again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.

- **Mute**, **Camera off** and **Leave** are under the video; **Share screen** on a computer.
- **Slides** beside the video follow the presenter. **Previous** and **Next** let you look on your own; **Back to the presenter** catches up.
- **Raise hand** to speak, **Chat** to write to everyone (not kept after the call).
- If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and **Join the call** opens that instead.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.</p><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-menu" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The menu</h2><p class="gd-p">Every office role has the same short menu: <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one <b class="gd-ui">More</b> for the rest of your work, <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> on Requests, <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters&#39; phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.</p><p class="gd-p">A <b class="gd-ui">More</b> page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Function</th><th scope="col">Your links, then More</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer service</td><td>Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur</td></tr><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button)</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-to-do" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">To do</h2><p class="gd-p">Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows your function, today&#39;s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Next up</b> is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service and Sales: <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for a reply</b> lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today&#39;s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every open task</b>: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. <b class="gd-ui">Sheet</b> opens the step-by-step procedure.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day&#39;s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">On a computer, press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:20.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.9%;top:52.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:72.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-work-a-task" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work a task</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open the working screen</b></td><td>Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Done</b></td><td>You finished it. It leaves the queue.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b></td><td>You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Escalate</b></td><td>It needs an Admin. Add why.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Hand over</b></td><td>Give it to someone else on the team.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b></td><td>Leave a note for whoever looks next.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-today" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Today</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press a booking number to open it. <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> takes you back to your tasks.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/today</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/700"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="700"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:24.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-documents-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents to sign</h2><p class="gd-p">Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The queue shows &quot;You have a document to sign&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-several-functions-switch-with-working-as" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Several functions? Switch with Working as</h2><p class="gd-p">If you cover more than one function, <b class="gd-ui">Working as</b> above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-scorecard" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your scorecard</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> (the <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b> tab).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/360"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="360"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.2%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:62.5%;top:58.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-clock-in-and-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Clock in and out</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press <b class="gd-ui">Clock in</b> on your home page when you start and <b class="gd-ui">Clock out</b> when you stop. <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b> shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-breaks-and-activity-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Breaks and activity (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Take breaks when you need them: there is no fixed length. Press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> next to the clock (a reason is optional) and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> when you are back. The timer shows how long the break has run; after 30 minutes you get a reminder and the Admins see it. Clocking out ends a break. Your breaks are on <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b>; only an Admin can change one, with the reason.</p><p class="gd-p">While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks <b class="gd-ui">Still there?</b>: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-first-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first days</h2><p class="gd-p">Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first (sign it on Welcome or Documents to sign), then the academy, then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show your WhatsApp groups (Sales: CARMA Closers and the CarmaCars Team; everyone else the Team group). Next to each link is your member tag, written for you as &quot;Name - Position&quot; (for example &quot;Darren - Sales&quot;), with <b class="gd-ui">Copy member tag</b> and the steps: open the group, tap its name, tap your own name (or Edit member tag), paste and save. Join each group and set the tag, then press <b class="gd-ui">I joined</b> and tick <b class="gd-ui">I set my member tag</b>: I joined does not go through without it.</p><p class="gd-p">Passed the Sales part of the academy while Sales is not your main role? Your home page shows the Sales group (CARMA Closers) too: join it and set your tag the same way.</p><p class="gd-p">No progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call&#39;s deck, the next call time and its link. <b class="gd-ui">Add to my calendar</b> adds the call every week.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> there, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-kpis-on-your-scorecard-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">KPIs by week</b> sits on <b class="gd-ui">My scorecard</b>: your role&#39;s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-schedule-hours-and-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your schedule, hours and pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b> shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Schedule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer service</td><td>6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b>, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares the payroll under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b>: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-townhall-s-30-minutes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall&#39;s 30 minutes</h2><p class="gd-p">The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press <b class="gd-ui">Join now</b> (from 15 minutes before), then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm I am in the call</b> on the Townhall page, or press <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b>: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? <b class="gd-ui">Tell yours</b> under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week&#39;s recording is listed on the Townhall page.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-breaks-quiet-hours-and-the-approval-gate-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet VA&#39;s approval.</li><li>Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.</li><li>Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.</li><li>Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall-card-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall card (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, <b class="gd-ui">Join / check in</b> (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-townhall-call-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall call in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Camera off</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Leave</b> are under the video; <b class="gd-ui">Share screen</b> on a computer.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Slides</b> beside the video follow the presenter. <b class="gd-ui">Previous</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> let you look on your own; <b class="gd-ui">Back to the presenter</b> catches up.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Raise hand</b> to speak, <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> to write to everyone (not kept after the call).</li><li>If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens that instead.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'start-here', 'start', null, '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars field staff: drivers, detailers, and drivers who also detail. You hand cars over, take them back, move them and shoot listing photos. Everything is on your phone. Your jobs are under **Field work** in the staff portal; if you also hold another function (Sales, for example), its pages are in the same menu.

### What you need

- Your phone, charged, with a data connection (photos and signatures save as you take them)
- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A car charger and a cloth for the camera lens

## Once you are hired

You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.

1. Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once your agreement is signed and the academy is passed).
2. In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as "Name - Position", for example "Ali - Field".

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email on your phone and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land on **Today**. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password.
3. In your browser''s menu, choose **Add to Home Screen**. The portal then opens full screen, like an app.
4. Open **Profile**, add your mobile number and press **Save my phone**.
5. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 4 92.3 78.3")

> Good to know: Recommended: on Profile, press **Set up two-step sign-in** and follow the steps with an authenticator app.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the right chapter in a sheet from the bottom of the screen; **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while a renter signs.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first, then the academy (Training), then your jobs. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and Today show the team''s WhatsApp group: join it, then press **I joined**.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.

## Work chats only

All work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. Questions, handovers, problems and customer details go in the group, so the whole team sees them and nothing is lost when someone is away. If a colleague or an Admin writes to you privately about work, answer in the group.
## Something to check on your record (release 48)

When something on your record looks wrong, a box opens on any page of the portal and says exactly what, with the box to fix it right there: your staff agreement waiting for your driver''s licence number or home address, a home address outside Ontario while you work in person in Toronto (fix it, or press It''s correct and say why), a licence that expires within 30 days (or has expired), pay details missing, a phone number that is not valid, or your WhatsApp member tag not confirmed. Press **Save** and the box checks again.

1. Your agreement waiting for something you give cannot be put off: once you save it, the agreement is made and appears under Documents to sign at once. The sign page says the same when nothing is ready to sign yet.
2. Anything else you can put off with **Remind me later**: it comes back after a day.

## Guide me

**Guide me** walks you through a job step by step while you do it: a pickup, a return or an expense. Press **Guide me** at the top (or **Guide me: a pickup**, **Guide me: a return** or **Guide me: an expense** on Today). A card points at the next thing to do, with Step X of Y; it moves on by itself once you have done it. **Back**, **Skip** and the cross (exit) are always there, and it picks up where you were if you leave the page. Tick **Keep Guide me on** to have it offer each time.
